  served from the staged copies of /app/vue.js and /app/vuetify.js.

## Setup required
  The three /app files must exist and be non-empty when the run starts; the
  staging step aborts the run otherwise. The served copies are asserted
  byte-identical to /app, so the implementation is established by working on
  those files in place on disk; nothing rebuilds or rebundles them before the
  page executes them. The page runs the library as plain classic scripts in a
  browser window: no module loader, no bundler, no Node — the UMD build must
  find Vue on the global. Headless Chromium and chromedriver are installed in
  the image, with Python 3.9 plus pytest and selenium driving them. The
  container'"'"'s entrypoint keeps a python -m http.server serving /app on port
  8000 alive, but the callers never request it: all contact with the
  implementation is through the filesystem staging described above.

