  The calling side, not the implementation, comprises: the pytest runner; the
  staging step that copies the three /app files into the served directory and
  writes their size/sha256 manifest; the two ephemeral HTTP servers rooted at
  the caller'"'"'s own directory (ports 8765 and 8766), one of which records each
  request path it serves; the headless Chromium browser driven through
  Selenium; and the served calendar page itself — its markup, the Vue mount,
  the events array, and the getEventName callback method. The implementation
  is exactly the three files under /app. The page, the servers, the staging,
  and the browser tooling are not rebuilt by the engineer.
