  A PHP web application served by Apache (php:7.4-apache image) with
  DocumentRoot set to /app. Callers reach it over HTTP at a base URL resolved
  from the APP_URL environment variable, defaulting to http://localhost:80,
  and issue GET requests against top-level PHP scripts at the document root:
      requests.get(BASE_URL + '"'"'/client-report.php'"'"',  params={...})
      requests.get(BASE_URL + '"'"'/backupjob-report.php'"'"', params={...})
      requests.get(BASE_URL + '"'"'/jobs.php'"'"',           params={...})
  The application source is staged into /app at image build time; composer
  dependencies are installed under /app/vendor, and the runtime entry for each
  route is the corresponding top-level script: /app/client-report.php,
  /app/backupjob-report.php, /app/jobs.php. Each script begins with
  `require_once('"'"'core/global.inc.php'"'"')` and reads request inputs from the
  query string. A SQLite catalog database is initialized at /app/bacula.db
  from /app/init_db.sql by the container entrypoint before Apache starts.

## Must provide
  /app/client-report.php      PHP route, served at /client-report.php
  /app/backupjob-report.php   PHP route, served at /backupjob-report.php
  /app/jobs.php               PHP route, served at /jobs.php

## Called as
  GET /client-report.php
    client_id  query parameter; a string
    period     query parameter; a string
  GET /backupjob-report.php
    backupjob_name  query parameter; a string
    period          query parameter; a string
  GET /jobs.php
    status            query parameter; a string
    job_type          query parameter; a string
    client_id         query parameter; a string
    orderby           query parameter; a string
    result_order_asc  query parameter; a string
  Each route is also called with no query parameters. Every parameter listed
  above is passed by the caller as an HTTP query-string parameter.

## Setup required
  APP_URL environment variable set to the service base URL (defaults to
  http://localhost:80 when unset). Apache with mod_rewrite enabled, serving
  /app as DocumentRoot with AllowOverride All, running PHP 7.4 with the pdo
  and pdo_sqlite extensions. The SQLite catalog database at /app/bacula.db
  must be initialized from /app/init_db.sql, and /app/application/view/cache
  must exist and be writable, before requests are served. The container
  entrypoint performs database initialization and starts Apache in the
  foreground; the service must be up and answering before report requests
  are issued.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side is a pytest runner that uses the Python `requests` library
  to issue HTTP GET requests against BASE_URL and to poll that URL until the
  service answers before issuing report requests. That runner, its readiness
  poll, and its HTTP client belong to the caller, not to the implementation;
