## Reached at
  Two PHP class files inside the Navigate CMS application tree staged at /app by
  the image build. Each caller loads one by absolute path under the PHP CLI
  interpreter /usr/local/bin/php (PHP 7.4) and calls a public static method on
  the class it defines:
      require_once '"'"'/app/lib/packages/extensions/extension.class.php'"'"';
      require_once '"'"'/app/lib/packages/themes/theme.class.php'"'"';
  The calling side pins ownership via ReflectionClass: it resolves
      realpath((new ReflectionClass('"'"'extension'"'"'))->getFileName())
      realpath((new ReflectionClass('"'"'theme'"'"'))->getFileName())
  and requires each defining file to sit inside the app tree rooted at /app, so
  both classes must be defined by these project-owned files, not by code placed
  elsewhere on the PHP include path. /usr/local/bin/php itself is the
  base-image interpreter, not project code.

## Must provide
  extension             PHP class (lowercase name), declared in
                        /app/lib/packages/extensions/extension.class.php
  extension::check_upload
                        public static method on class extension
  theme                 PHP class (lowercase name), declared in
                        /app/lib/packages/themes/theme.class.php
  theme::check_upload   public static method on class theme

## Called as
  extension::check_upload($file_upload, $extension_name)
  theme::check_upload($file_upload, $theme_name)

      $file_upload     1st positional argument; a PHP associative array in
                       $_FILES-entry shape with the string keys:
                         '"'"'type'"'"'      a string
                         '"'"'name'"'"'      a string; callers pass '"'"'<package name>.zip'"'"'
                         '"'"'tmp_name'"'"'  a string; a filesystem path to an uploaded
                                     archive file created by the caller
      $extension_name  2nd positional argument; a string, the package name
      $theme_name      2nd positional argument; a string, the package name

  The caller builds each package archive itself in a scratch directory: an
  extension archive holds a '"'"'<package name>.plugin'"'"' entry and a theme archive
  holds a '"'"'<package name>.theme'"'"' entry (a text file; callers pass archives both
  with and without it), plus the remaining package files, which callers place
  at the archive root and in nested subdirectories. The second argument carries
  the same package-name stem that forms that metadata entry'"'"'s name.

## Setup required
  In the PHP process that loads the class files, the calling script first
  defines
      define('"'"'NAVIGATE_PATH'"'"', '"'"'/app'"'"');
      define('"'"'NAVIGATE_PRIVATE'"'"', '"'"'<writable scratch directory>'"'"');
  and pre-creates NAVIGATE_PRIVATE and NAVIGATE_PRIVATE . '"'"'/tmp'"'"'. Loading
  theme.class.php runs a chain of require_once statements that resolve further
  retained project files relative to NAVIGATE_PATH, so the constant must be
  defined before the load and point at the app tree. Before loading, the
  calling script also defines the global functions
  core_recursive_file_search($dir, $pattern) and core_remove_folder($dir); when
  the class methods reference those names at call time, they resolve to the
  caller'"'"'s definitions.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner constructs each package archive in a temporary directory,
  writes a generated PHP driver script to a temp file, and runs it through
  subprocess as `/usr/local/bin/php <script>`. The driver script supplies the
  constants, the stand-in global helpers (core_recursive_file_search walks a
  directory tree and collects file paths matching a preg pattern;
  core_remove_folder removes a directory tree), the $file_upload array, and the
  static call itself. All of that — runner, driver script, constants,
  stand-ins, and the scratch archives — belongs to the calling side and is not
  part of the implementation.
