    other environment variable or on the caller'"'"'s working directory.
  - Constructing the '"'"'mysql'"'"', '"'"'mariadb'"'"' and '"'"'sqlite'"'"' QueryGenerators must not
    require a running database server; no connection is opened for those calls.
    The sqlite end-to-end route needs the native driver resolvable from
    /app/node_modules/sqlite3 (preinstalled dependency) and opens the database
    at '"'"':memory:'"'"'.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side is a pytest-driven runner that writes a temporary Node
  script into /tmp, executes `/usr/local/bin/node <script>` through
  `subprocess` with the scrubbed environment, parses the last stdout line of
  the script as JSON, and first proves the interpreter actually executes an
  arithmetic computation before trusting any script output. That runner, its
  temporary scripts, its JSON parsing and its interpreter canary belong to the
  caller and are not part of the implementation; the sqlite3 driver and every
  other package under /app/node_modules are dependencies, not implementation.
