## Reached at
  A prebuilt Go executable at the absolute path `/app/nuclei`. It is produced by
  the image build from the projectdiscovery/nuclei v3.1.0 Go module cloned into
  `/app`, via:
      go build -o nuclei ./cmd/nuclei
  A caller reaches it by spawning that path as a subprocess:
      subprocess.run(["/app/nuclei"] + args + ["-duc", "-no-color"], ...)
  Both calling suites resolve the binary through the same constant `/app/nuclei`;
  the runner treats a missing binary at that path as a hard failure, not a skip.

## Must provide
  Executable artifact at `/app/nuclei`, built from the Go module rooted at `/app`
  (entry package `./cmd/nuclei`).
  CLI surface the binary must accept:
    -w <path>        workflow file path
    -t <path>        template file path
    -u <url>         target URL
    -code            boolean switch
    -timeout <n>     timeout value
    -sign            verb (used with -t)
    -version         version verb
    -h               help verb
    -duc             always appended by the runner
    -no-color        always appended by the runner

## Called as
  Every invocation is a subprocess of the form:
      ["/app/nuclei"] + <args> + ["-duc", "-no-color"]
  run with a signing-keypair environment (see Setup required). The arg vectors
  callers use:
      ["-w", <workflow-path>, "-u", <url>, "-timeout", "10"]
      ["-w", <workflow-path>, "-u", <url>, "-code", "-timeout", "10"]
      ["-t", <template-path>, "-u", <url>, "-code", "-timeout", "10"]
      ["-sign", "-t", <template-path>]
      ["-version"]
      ["-h"]
  Input shapes:
    -w / -t   a string; an absolute filesystem path to a YAML file the caller authored
    -u        a string; a URL
    -code     a boolean switch (present or absent in the arg vector)
    -timeout  a string giving a numeric value
  The YAML files the caller authors and passes by path:
    workflow file   has a `workflows:` section; each entry references a template by
                    path under a `template:` key, optionally with `subtemplates:`
                    and `matchers:`/`name:` nesting
    template file   an `http:` template (method/path/matchers) or a `code:` template
                    (an `engine:` list and a `source:` block)
  The `-sign -t <path>` invocation depends on the keypair environment variables.

## Setup required
  For the `-sign` invocation, two environment variables must be set and must point
  at a signing certificate and private key:
    NUCLEI_USER_CERTIFICATE   path to a certificate file
    NUCLEI_USER_PRIVATE_KEY   path to a private key file
  The caller supplies these; the harness restores the keypair at a fixed location
  so it cannot be replaced out from under the run. The binary must be present at
  `/app/nuclei` (the image build prebuilds it; the run script rebuilds it via
  `go build -o nuclei ./cmd/nuclei` when absent).

## Test harness boundary
  These belong to the calling side, not to the implementation, and must not be
  rebuilt: a pytest runner that spawns the binary via `subprocess.run`, always
  appending `-duc` and `-no-color` and setting the keypair environment; a helper
  that authors the workflow and template YAML input files by writing them to a
  temporary directory and returning their absolute paths; a helper that invokes
  the `-sign` verb with `-t <path>` and the keypair environment; a temporary
  threaded HTTP server bound to 127.0.0.1 on an ephemeral port, used as the live
  target for `-u`, that records the requests it receives; and helpers that read
  back the run'"'"'s captured output and the server'"'"'s recorded requests. The signing
  keypair is harness-supplied. None of these are part of the implementation under
  reconstruction.
