- **Side effects and interactions:** The child'"'"'s stdout and stderr are piped to the parent process'"'"'s stdout and stderr. Each `start` records the spawned child as the export surface'"'"'s `defaultInstance`, replacing the previous one; before any `start`, no instance is recorded. If no file exists at the default binary location at call time, the module announces via console output that it is falling back to the global chromedriver bin and instead launches a command named `chromedriver` resolved through `PATH` (the retained module-level statement above this region has already prepended the binary'"'"'s directory to `PATH`). `stop()` terminates the currently recorded instance; with none recorded it does nothing.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Instance recording happens during the `start` call, before either return; in the promise form the port wait begins after the spawn and settles with the same child object. Repeated `start` calls overwrite the recorded instance; `stop()` acts only on the most recent one.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained. The range spans whole export assignments through the end of the file. The retained text immediately above (the complete `PATH` statement) opens nothing the region must close, and no text follows it. Reconnection note, not a syntactic obligation: this region follows the retained `PATH` statement and the region r0 definition whose port-resolution result its promise branch consumes.
