## Called as
  ui.fileLoaded(new LocalFile(ui, data, title, temp))
      1st positional (data)  — a string (mxfile/diagram XML)
      2nd positional (title)  — a string
      3rd positional (temp)  — a boolean
  ui.getCurrentFile()
      no arguments
  ui.updateUserElement()
      no arguments; reads ui.gitHub.getUser().displayName and ui.gitHub.isAuthorized()
  ui.gitHub                 set to a plain object: `{ getUser: function() { return { displayName: <string> }; }, isAuthorized: function() { ...; } }`
  ui.userElement.click()
      no arguments
  ui.actions.get('"'"'layers'"'"').funct()
      no arguments
  model.add(model.getRoot(), new mxCell(name))
      1st positional — the model root; 2nd positional — an mxCell whose 1st constructor arg is a string (layer name)
  model.beginUpdate() / model.endUpdate()
      no arguments, wrapped around the model mutation
  ui.editor.graph.getModel()  / getModel().getRoot()
      no arguments
  new NewDialog(ui, compact, showName, callback, createOnly, cancelCallback, ... further positionals ...)
      1st (ui)         — the App instance
      2nd (compact)    — a boolean
      3rd (showName)   — a boolean
      4th (callback)   — a function or null
      5th (createOnly) — a boolean
      6th (cancelCallback) — a function or null
      subsequent positionals — callback functions or null (template-search result callbacks, custom-template category callback)
  ui.showDialog(dlg.container, width, height, modal, closable)
      1st — the dialog'"'"'s container element; 2nd, 3rd — numbers (pixel dimensions); 4th, 5th — booleans
  ui.hideDialog(true)
      1st positional — a boolean
  new RevisionDialog(ui, revs, restoreFn)
      1st (ui)        — the App instance
      2nd (revs)     — an array of revision objects; each revision is a plain object with `modifiedDate` (number), `fileSize` (string), `lastModifyingUserName` (string), `getXml: function(ok, err)` where `ok` is a function
      3rd (restoreFn) — a function taking an `xml` argument
  dlg.init()
      no arguments (RevisionDialog)
  rows[i].click() / element.click()
      no arguments (DOM dispatch on dialog-internal rows/buttons found by traversing dlg.container)
  compareBtn.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('"'"'pointerdown'"'"', {bubbles: true}))
  compareBtn.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('"'"'pointerup'"'"', {bubbles: true}))
      a PointerEvent dispatched on a button located by its title attribute (string containing '"'"'compare'"'"')
  input.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('"'"'keydown'"'"', {keyCode: 13, which: 13, bubbles: true}))
      a KeyboardEvent dispatched on a search input located by its placeholder attribute
  mxResources.get('"'"'pageNotFound'"'"')
      1st positional — a string (resource key)
  graph.getChildVertices(graph.getDefaultParent())
      no arguments on getDefaultParent; the returned array is indexed, and
      graph.convertValueToString(vertex) takes the vertex element as 1st positional

## Setup required
  The browser binary must be the headless Chromium at /usr/bin/chromium with its
  driver at /usr/local/bin/chromedriver. The page is loaded over the file
  protocol with `--allow-file-access-from-files`; the application boots from its
  own source tree on disk under /app/src/main/webapp/, not from an HTTP fetch.
  The CDP pre-script (`Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument`) must be installed
  before `driver.get(APP_PAGE)` so it runs in the page'"'"'s main world before any
  page script: it captures the `App` instance into `window.__vsb_ui` and wraps the
  `Element.prototype.innerHTML`, `HTMLElement.prototype.innerText`, and
  `Node.prototype.textContent` setters with a recorder that delegates to the
  original native setters. Readiness is polled until `window.__vsb_ui` is set and
  the instance exposes `fname`, `actions`, and `editor` with a rendered
  `.geDiagramContainer`. The loaded page href must start with
  `file:///app/src/main/webapp/index.html` and the loaded `<script src>` list must
  include the three app-tree module paths above by absolute path; an aliased or
  replaced source set is rejected.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner creates a headless Chromium driver, injects the CDP pre-script,
  loads the app page, polls it to readiness, and then drives the application by
  executing synchronous in-page JavaScript blocks against the captured `ui`
  instance and the global constructors the app'"'"'s own source declares. The runner,
  the driver setup, the CDP pre-script, the recorder/canary helper functions, the
  in-page drive scripts, and the resource-key lookups all belong to the calling
  side, not to the implementation; they are the means of reaching the
  application'"'"'s public API and observing the DOM writes its code performs. The
  implementation is the draw.io application source tree under
  /app/src/main/webapp/ as loaded by its own dev bootstrap.
